# RAM never written by stock fw (GWemu canary probe 2026-10-16, 2 identical runs: boot, clock, every game-select variant played briefly; sleep images / nvram UNVERIFIED)
0x0000b7c0 data itcm_unused                           # to 0x00010000 (18496 B): past the last itcm_overlay_load copy (menu UI ends at 0x0000b7c0)
#   AXI 0x240d3560-0x240d6000 (10912 B; now our linker RAM), 0x240fc120-0x240fd000 (3808 B), 0x2401f320-0x24020000 (3296 B),
#       0x240a50f0-0x240a5c20 and 0x240b7cf0-0x240b8820 (2864 B each), 0x24090c40-0x24091040 (1024 B),
#       0x240dce00-0x240dd000 and 0x240e5e00-0x240e6000 (512 B each) also unused
#   No DTCM, AHB or SRD block >= 512 B is unused.
#   Stock-only probe (ram_probe.py --stock, 2026-10-16) agrees and adds AXI 0x240ff0c0-0x24100000 (3904 B), 0x240ece00-0x240ed000 (512 B)
#       and DTCM 0x2001b220-0x2001b340 (288 B). It paints our linker RAM region too: stock owns all of it except 0x240ece00-0x240ed000.
#   Our linker RAM region used to be 0x240ec524-0x240fcef8, inside app_state_loz2_en/app_state_loz2_jp: app_state_buffers_clear
#       zeroes those at boot, after our init, and the timer's runtime memcpy_inflate then overwrote 13520 B of saved LoZ2 JP state
#       (LoZ2 JP hangs on resume; stock doesn't). Per-game GWemu runs: only LoZ2 EN/JP write that range. Our RAM now starts at
#       0x240d3560 (scripts/device_from_patch_params.py), which lc=0 LZMA (5.5 KB heap) makes fit.
# --- generated: names shared with the other G&W firmware (HAL/SDK/runtime matched by code) and session RE
